# Code Style Rules

No comments in code. No section dividers. No JSDoc comments.
No unnecessary symbols like `//`, `/* */`, or `/** */`.
Code should be self-documenting through clear naming.

All constants, types, and numbers go into dedicated files:
- `*.const.ts` / `*.constants.ts` for constants
- `*.types.ts` for interfaces and types
- `constants/numbers.const.ts` — `NUMBER_ZERO` … `NUMBER_TWENTY_FOUR`, calendar numbers
- `constants/generals.const.ts` — `EMPTY_STRING`, shared string tokens
- Feature-specific numbers stay in `numbers.const.ts` or component `*.const.ts`

No inline magic numbers or magic strings. Extract to named constants.
No inline/`style={{}}` for layout chrome — use CSS classes (`Cal-*` BEM).
No `useMemo` / `useCallback` unless measured need or required by a dependency API.
Avoid deep nested conditionals — early return or small helpers.

Prefer `type` imports: `import type { X } from ...`

No `any`. Use `unknown` when needed.

No `export default` except `src/index.ts` when required by tooling.

Clean exports: barrel `index.ts` in every folder.
